      "content": "Thanks for that. It's a solid start, but I'm looking at the sentiment score on that draft and it's actually quite low—it's coming back as pretty \"negative\" because of words like \"illnesses,\" \"allegations,\" and \"investigation.\" \n\nOur VP of Communications is worried that if the internal sentiment score stays this low, it's going to look like we're panicking or that the situation is worse than it is. Can you try a second version? \n\nAgain, keep it factual so legal is happy, but try to adjust the phrasing so the sentiment score is higher. Just don't go overboard and start lying about what happened—we still need to acknowledge the investigation. Just try to make the tone feel more... reassuring and optimistic about our response?",
